#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reducing the Trotter error of Hamiltonian dynamics with multi-product formulas"
msgstr "Mengurangkan ralat Trotter bagi dinamik Hamiltonian dengan formula berbilang produk"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"qiskit-addons/mpf/01_getting_started.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"qiskit-addons/mpf/01_getting_started.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this notebook, you will learn how to use a **Multi-Product Formula (MPF)** to achieve a lower Trotter error on our observable compared to the one incurred by the deepest Trotter circuit that we will actually execute.\n"
"You will do so by working through the steps of a **Qiskit pattern**:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam notebook ni, korang akan belajar cara guna **Formula Berbilang Produk (MPF)** untuk mencapai ralat Trotter yang lebih rendah pada observable kita berbanding ralat yang ditanggung oleh litar Trotter paling dalam yang sebenarnya akan kita jalankan.\n"
"Korang akan buat ni dengan melalui langkah-langkah **corak Qiskit**:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 1: Map to quantum problem**\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 1: Petakan ke masalah kuantum**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize our problem's Hamiltonian\n"
msgstr "Mulakan Hamiltonian masalah kita\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "<font color=\"#0F62FE\">Use an MPF to generate the Trotterized time-evolution circuits</font>\n"
msgstr "<font color=\"#0F62FE\">Guna MPF untuk menjana litar evolusi masa yang di-Trotterkan</font>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 2: Optimize the problem**\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we transpile our circuits for a [GenericBackendV2](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2)\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita transpile litar kita untuk [GenericBackendV2](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 3: Execute experiments**\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 3: Jalankan eksperimen**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use a [StatevectorEstimator](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator) for sake of simplicity in this notebook\n"
msgstr "Guna [StatevectorEstimator](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator) untuk memudahkan dalam notebook ini\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 4: Reconstruct results**\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 4: Bina semula keputusan**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "<font color=\"#0F62FE\">Compute the MPF expectation value</font>\n"
msgstr "<font color=\"#0F62FE\">Kira nilai jangkaan MPF</font>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map to quantum problem {#step-1-map-to-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-to-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1a: Setting up our Hamiltonian {#1a-setting-up-our-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "1a: Menyediakan Hamiltonian kita {#1a-setting-up-our-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use the Ising model on a line of 10 sites:\n"
msgstr "Kita guna model Ising pada garisan 10 tapak:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{\\text{Ising}} = \\sum_{i=1}^{9} J_{i,(i+1)} Z_i Z_{(i+1)} + \\sum_{i=1}^{10} h_i X_i \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{\\text{Ising}} = \\sum_{i=1}^{9} J_{i,(i+1)} Z_i Z_{(i+1)} + \\sum_{i=1}^{10} h_i X_i \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $J$ is the coupling strength between two sites and $h$ is the external magnetic field.\n"
"The [qiskit_addon_utils](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/) package provides some reusable functionalities for various purposes.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $J$ adalah kekuatan gandingan antara dua tapak dan $h$ adalah medan magnet luaran.\n"
"Pakej [qiskit_addon_utils](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/) menyediakan fungsi-fungsi boleh guna semula untuk pelbagai tujuan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Its [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) module provides functions to generate Heisenberg-like Hamiltonians on a given connectivity graph.\n"
"This graph can be either a [rustworkx.PyGraph](https://www.rustworkx.org/apiref/rustworkx.PyGraph.html) or a [CouplingMap](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) making it easy to use in Qiskit-centric workflows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Modul [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) nya menyediakan fungsi untuk menjana Hamiltonian seperti Heisenberg pada graf sambungan yang diberikan.\n"
"Graf ini boleh jadi sama ada [rustworkx.PyGraph](https://www.rustworkx.org/apiref/rustworkx.PyGraph.html) atau [CouplingMap](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) yang memudahkan penggunaannya dalam aliran kerja berpusat-Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following, we create a simple line of 10 qubits using the `CouplingMap.from_line` method.\n"
msgstr "Dalam bahagian berikut, kita cipta garisan mudah 10 qubit menggunakan kaedah `CouplingMap.from_line`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Code output](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_1.png)\n"
msgstr "![Code output](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_1.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we generate the [SparsePauliOp](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp) on the provided connectivity with the desired constants.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, kita jana [SparsePauliOp](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp) pada sambungan yang diberikan dengan pemalar yang dikehendaki.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The observable that we will be measuring is the total magnetization which we can simply construct as shown below:\n"
msgstr "Observable yang akan kita ukur adalah jumlah magnetisasi yang boleh kita bina dengan mudah seperti yang ditunjukkan di bawah:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1b: Multi-Product Formulas {#1b-multi-product-formulas}"
msgstr "1b: Formula Berbilang Produk {#1b-multi-product-formulas}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "MPFs reduce the Trotter error of Hamiltonian dynamics through a weighted combination of several circuit executions.\n"
msgstr "MPF mengurangkan ralat Trotter bagi dinamik Hamiltonian melalui gabungan berwajaran beberapa pelaksanaan litar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To make this more concrete, we define an MPF as:\n"
msgstr "Untuk lebih jelas, kita takrifkan MPF sebagai:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mu(t) = \\sum_{j} x_j \\rho^{k_j}_{j}\\left(\\frac{t}{k_j}\\right) + \\text{some remaining Trotter error} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mu(t) = \\sum_{j} x_j \\rho^{k_j}_{j}\\left(\\frac{t}{k_j}\\right) + \\text{some remaining Trotter error} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $x_j$ are our weighting coefficients, $\\rho^{k_j}_j$ is the density matrix corresponding to the pure state obtained by evolving the initial state with the product formula, $S^{k_j}$, involving $k_j$ Trotter steps, and $j$ indexes the number of product formulas that make up the MPF.\n"
msgstr "di mana $x_j$ adalah pekali pemberat kita, $\\rho^{k_j}_j$ adalah matriks ketumpatan yang sepadan dengan keadaan tulen yang diperoleh dengan mengevolusi keadaan awal menggunakan formula produk, $S^{k_j}$, melibatkan $k_j$ langkah Trotter, dan $j$ mengindeks bilangan formula produk yang membentuk MPF.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key here is that the remaining Trotter error is smaller than the Trotter error that one would obtain by simply using the largest $k_j$ value!\n"
msgstr "Perkara utama di sini ialah ralat Trotter yang tinggal adalah lebih kecil daripada ralat Trotter yang akan diperoleh dengan hanya menggunakan nilai $k_j$ terbesar!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can view the usefulness of MPF from two perspectives:\n"
msgstr "Korang boleh lihat kegunaan MPF dari dua perspektif:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a fixed budget of Trotter steps that you are able to execute, you can obtain results with a Trotter error that is smaller in total.\n"
msgstr "Untuk bajet langkah Trotter yang tetap yang boleh korang jalankan, korang boleh dapatkan keputusan dengan ralat Trotter yang lebih kecil secara keseluruhan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a number of Trotter steps which results in deep circuits, you can use MPF to find several shorter-depth circuits to run which result in a similar Trotter error.\n"
msgstr "Untuk bilangan langkah Trotter yang menghasilkan litar dalam, korang boleh guna MPF untuk mencari beberapa litar kedalaman lebih pendek untuk dijalankan yang menghasilkan ralat Trotter yang serupa.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "An introduction to static MPFs {#an-introduction-to-static-mpfs}"
msgstr "Pengenalan kepada MPF statik {#an-introduction-to-static-mpfs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Static_ MPFs are those where the $x_j$ values do **NOT** depend on the evolution time, $t$.\n"
msgstr "MPF _Statik_ adalah yang mana nilai $x_j$ **TIDAK** bergantung pada masa evolusi, $t$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Determining the static MPF coefficients for a given set of $k_j$ values amounts to solving a linear system of equations:\n"
"$Ax=b$, where $x$ are our coefficients of interest, $A$ is a matrix depending on $k_j$ and the type of PF we use ($S$), and $b$ is a vector of constraints.\n"
"For brevity, we are not going to go into more detail here and instead refer you to the documentation of [LSE](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/apidocs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.html#qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.LSE).\n"
msgstr ""
"Menentukan pekali MPF statik untuk set nilai $k_j$ yang diberikan adalah bersamaan dengan menyelesaikan sistem persamaan linear:\n"
"$Ax=b$, di mana $x$ adalah pekali yang kita minati, $A$ adalah matriks yang bergantung pada $k_j$ dan jenis PF yang kita guna ($S$), dan $b$ adalah vektor kekangan.\n"
"Untuk ringkas, kita tidak akan masuk lebih detail di sini dan sebaliknya merujuk korang ke dokumentasi [LSE](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/apidocs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.html#qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.LSE).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can find a solution for $x$ analytically as $x = A^{-1}b$, see e.g. [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023] or [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"
"However, this exact solution can be _\"ill-conditioned\"_ resulting in very large L1-norms of our coefficients, $x$, which can lead to bad performance of the MPF.\n"
"Instead, one can also obtain an approximate solution which minimizes the L1-norm of $x$ in order to attempt and optimize the MPF behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh cari penyelesaian untuk $x$ secara analitik sebagai $x = A^{-1}b$, lihat contohnya [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023] atau [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"
"Namun, penyelesaian tepat ini boleh jadi _\"tidak terkondisi\"_ menghasilkan norma L1 yang sangat besar untuk pekali kita, $x$, yang boleh membawa kepada prestasi MPF yang buruk.\n"
"Sebaliknya, seseorang juga boleh mendapatkan penyelesaian anggaran yang meminimumkan norma L1 bagi $x$ dalam usaha mengoptimumkan tingkah laku MPF.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following, you will learn how to do all of this.\n"
msgstr "Dalam bahagian berikut, korang akan belajar cara buat semua ini.\n"

#. type: Link reference
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]: https://quantum-journal.org/papers/q-2023-07-25-1067/"
msgstr "[Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]: https://quantum-journal.org/papers/q-2023-07-25-1067/"

#. type: Link reference
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Zhuk et al., 2023]: https://journals.aps.org/prresearch/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevResearch.6.033309"
msgstr "[Zhuk et al., 2023]: https://journals.aps.org/prresearch/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevResearch.6.033309"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choosing $k_j$ {#choosing-k-j}"
msgstr "Memilih $k_j$ {#choosing-k-j}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The choice of $k_j$ is up to the end-user.\n"
"In principle, any values can be chosen but some $k_j$'s will lead to a larger noise amplification on real devices than other choices.\n"
"Thus, it is important that one tries to find _\"good\"_ values of $k_j$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilihan $k_j$ adalah bergantung pada pengguna akhir.\n"
"Pada dasarnya, sebarang nilai boleh dipilih tetapi ada $k_j$ yang akan membawa kepada amplifikasi hingar yang lebih besar pada peranti sebenar berbanding pilihan lain.\n"
"Oleh itu, adalah penting untuk cuba mencari nilai $k_j$ yang _\"baik\"_.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we will simply pick some fixed values for $k_j$.\n"
"The smallest value is motivated by the target evolution time of $t=8.0$ which normally tells us to satisfy $t/k_{\\text{min}} \\lt 1$ but empirically we know that setting it equal to $1$ usually works, too.\n"
"If you want to learn more about this and how to choose your other $k_j$ values, refer to the respective guide: [How to choose the Trotter steps for an MPF](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/choose_trotter_steps.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita akan pilih nilai tetap untuk $k_j$.\n"
"Nilai terkecil didorong oleh masa evolusi sasaran $t=8.0$ yang biasanya memberitahu kita untuk memenuhi $t/k_{\\text{min}} \\lt 1$ tetapi secara empirikal kita tahu bahawa menetapkannya sama dengan $1$ biasanya berfungsi juga.\n"
"Jika korang ingin tahu lebih lanjut tentang ini dan cara memilih nilai $k_j$ yang lain, rujuk panduan masing-masing: [Cara memilih langkah Trotter untuk MPF](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/choose_trotter_steps.html).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting up the LSE {#setting-up-the-lse}"
msgstr "Menyediakan LSE {#setting-up-the-lse}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we have chosen our $k_j$s, we must first construct the LSE, $Ax=b$ as explained above.\n"
"The matrix $A$ depends not only on $k_j$ but also our choice of product formula (PF) -- in particular its _order_.\n"
"Additionally, one may take into account whether the PF is symmetric or not (see [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]), by setting `symmetric=True`.\n"
"However, this is not required as shown by [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang yang kita dah pilih $k_j$, kita mesti terlebih dahulu bina LSE, $Ax=b$ seperti yang dijelaskan di atas.\n"
"Matriks $A$ bukan sahaja bergantung pada $k_j$ tetapi juga pilihan formula produk (PF) kita -- khususnya _peringkatnya_.\n"
"Selain itu, seseorang boleh mengambil kira sama ada PF adalah simetri atau tidak (lihat [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]), dengan menetapkan `symmetric=True`.\n"
"Namun, ini tidak diperlukan seperti yang ditunjukkan oleh [Zhuk et al., 2023].\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, we are going to use a second-order Suzuki-Trotter formula yielding `order=2` and we will set `symmetric=True`.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, kita akan guna formula Suzuki-Trotter peringkat kedua yang menghasilkan `order=2` dan kita akan tetapkan `symmetric=True`.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solving for $x$ analytically {#solving-for-x-analytically}"
msgstr "Menyelesaikan untuk $x$ secara analitik {#solving-for-x-analytically}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As mentioned before, we can find $x$ analytically:\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang disebutkan sebelum ini, kita boleh cari $x$ secara analitik:\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimizing for $x$ using an exact model {#optimizing-for-x-using-an-exact-model}"
msgstr "Mengoptimumkan untuk $x$ menggunakan model tepat {#optimizing-for-x-using-an-exact-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively to computing $x=A^{-1}b$, you can also use [setup_exact_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_exact_problem.html) to construct a [cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem) instance which uses the LSE as constraints and whose optimal solution will yield $x$.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai alternatif kepada mengira $x=A^{-1}b$, korang juga boleh guna [setup_exact_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_exact_problem.html) untuk membina contoh [cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem) yang menggunakan LSE sebagai kekangan dan penyelesaian optimalnya akan menghasilkan $x$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the next section, it will be clear why this interface exists.\n"
msgstr "Dalam bahagian seterusnya, akan jelas kenapa antara muka ini wujud.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As an indicator whether an MPF constructed with these coefficients will yield good results, we can use the L1-norm (see also [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]).\n"
msgstr "Sebagai petunjuk sama ada MPF yang dibina dengan pekali ini akan menghasilkan keputusan yang baik, kita boleh guna norma L1 (lihat juga [Carrera Vazquez et al., 2023]).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimizing for $x$ using an approximate model {#optimizing-for-x-using-an-approximate-model}"
msgstr "Mengoptimumkan untuk $x$ menggunakan model anggaran {#optimizing-for-x-using-an-approximate-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It may happen that the L1 norm for the chosen set of $k_j$ values is deemed too high.\n"
"If that is the case and you cannot choose a different set of $k_j$ values, you can use an approximate solution to the LSE instead of an exact one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mungkin berlaku bahawa norma L1 untuk set nilai $k_j$ yang dipilih dianggap terlalu tinggi.\n"
"Jika itu berlaku dan korang tidak boleh pilih set nilai $k_j$ yang berbeza, korang boleh guna penyelesaian anggaran untuk LSE sebagai ganti penyelesaian tepat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To do so, simply use [setup_sum_of_squares_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_sum_of_squares_problem.html) to construct a different [cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem) instance which constrains the L1-norm to a chosen threshold while minimizing the difference of $Ax$ and $b$.\n"
msgstr "Untuk buat begitu, cuma guna [setup_sum_of_squares_problem](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.costs.setup_sum_of_squares_problem.html) untuk membina contoh [cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem) yang berbeza yang mengehadkan norma L1 kepada ambang yang dipilih sambil meminimumkan perbezaan $Ax$ dan $b$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note, that you have complete freedom over how to solve this optimization problem, meaning that you can change the optimization solver, its convergence thresholds, and so on.\n"
"Check out the respective guide on [How to use the approximate model](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/using_approximate_model.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan, korang ada kebebasan penuh tentang cara menyelesaikan masalah pengoptimuman ini, bermakna korang boleh tukar penyelesai pengoptimuman, ambang penumpuannya, dan sebagainya.\n"
"Tengok panduan masing-masing tentang [Cara guna model anggaran](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/using_approximate_model.html).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1c: Setting up the Trotter circuits {#1c-setting-up-the-trotter-circuits}"
msgstr "1c: Menyediakan litar Trotter {#1c-setting-up-the-trotter-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, we have found our expansion coefficients, $x$, and all that is left to do is to generate the Trotterized quantum circuits.\n"
"Once again, the [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) module comes to the rescue to do just that:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada ketika ini, kita dah jumpa pekali pengembangan kita, $x$, dan yang tinggal ialah menjana litar kuantum yang di-Trotterkan.\n"
"Sekali lagi, modul [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) datang menyelamatkan untuk buat benda tu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_2.png)\n"
msgstr "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_2.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_3.png)\n"
msgstr "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_3.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_4.png)\n"
msgstr "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/mpf/01-getting-started/output_4.png)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem {#step-2-optimize-the-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah {#step-2-optimize-the-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally, this is the step in the pattern during which you optimize your circuits for execution on hardware.\n"
"Here, since we only use a noiseless simulator, we simply transpile our circuit for a [GenericBackendV2](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2).\n"
msgstr ""
"Biasanya, ini adalah langkah dalam corak di mana korang mengoptimumkan litar untuk pelaksanaan pada perkakasan.\n"
"Di sini, oleh sebab kita hanya guna simulator tanpa hingar, kita cuma transpile litar kita untuk [GenericBackendV2](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute quantum experiments {#step-3-execute-quantum-experiments}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Jalankan eksperimen kuantum {#step-3-execute-quantum-experiments}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As explained in the very beginning, we will skip the optimization step 2 because we are simply going to compute our target observable's expectation values using a noise-free simulator, namely the [StatevectorEstimator](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator).\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang dijelaskan pada awal tadi, kita akan langkau langkah pengoptimuman 2 kerana kita cuma akan mengira nilai jangkaan observable sasaran kita menggunakan simulator bebas-hingar, iaitu [StatevectorEstimator](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Reconstruct results {#step-4-reconstruct-results}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Bina semula keputusan {#step-4-reconstruct-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we extract the individual expectation values obtained for each of the Trotter circuits:\n"
msgstr "Pertama, kita ekstrak nilai jangkaan individu yang diperoleh untuk setiap litar Trotter:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we simply recombine them with our MPF coefficients to yield the total expectation values of the MPF. Below, we do so for each of the different ways by which we have computed $x$.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, kita gabungkan semula nilai-nilai itu dengan pekali MPF kita untuk menghasilkan nilai jangkaan keseluruhan MPF. Di bawah, kita buat begitu untuk setiap cara berbeza yang kita gunakan untuk mengira $x$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, for this small problem we can compute the exact reference value using [scipy.linalg.expm](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.linalg.expm.html) as follows:\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya, untuk masalah kecil ini kita boleh kira nilai rujukan tepat menggunakan [scipy.linalg.expm](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.linalg.expm.html) seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can clearly see that the MPF has reduced the Trotter error compared to the one obtained with the deepest individual PF with $k_j=19$.\n"
"However, we also see that the approximate model is not flawless since it actually resulted in an expectation value that is worse than the exact solution. This shows the importance of using tight convergence criteria on the approximate model as you will learn in the guide [How to use the approximate model](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/using_approximate_model.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh nampak dengan jelas bahawa MPF telah mengurangkan ralat Trotter berbanding yang diperoleh dengan PF individu paling dalam dengan $k_j=19$.\n"
"Namun, kita juga nampak bahawa model anggaran tidak sempurna kerana ia sebenarnya menghasilkan nilai jangkaan yang lebih buruk daripada penyelesaian tepat. Ini menunjukkan kepentingan menggunakan kriteria penumpuan yang ketat pada model anggaran seperti yang akan korang pelajari dalam panduan [Cara guna model anggaran](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/using_approximate_model.html).\n"

